alwaysApply: true

rules:

- section: Naming Conventions content: |

  ## 1. Variables and Functions

  - Use camelCase for variable and function names
  - Names must be descriptive and meaningful
  - Avoid single-letter variables except for loop counters like `i`

  ```typescript
  // Good
  const userProfile = getUserProfile();

  // Bad
  const up = getUP();
  ```

  ## 2. Components

  - Use PascalCase for React components
  - Component names should clearly express their purpose

  ```typescript
  // Good
  const UserProfileCard = () => { ... }

  // Bad
  const profile = () => { ... }
  ```

  ## 3. Types and Interfaces

  - Use PascalCase
  - Prefix interfaces with `I` if it clarifies meaning

  ```typescript
  type UserData = { ... }
  interface IUserAuthProps { ... }
  ```

  ## 4. Constants

  - Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants

  ```typescript
  const MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3;
  ```

- section: Code Formatting content: |

  ## 1. Indentation

  - 2 spaces, no tabs

  ## 2. Line Length

  - Maximum 100 characters per line

  ## 3. Spacing

  ```typescript
  // Good
  const sum = a + b;
  const items = [1, 2, 3];

  // Bad
  const sum = a + b;
  const items = [1, 2, 3];
  ```

  ## 4. Curly Braces

  ```typescript
  // Good
  if (condition) {
    doSomething();
  }

  // Bad
  if (condition) doSomething();
  ```

  ## 5. Object and Array Formatting

  ```typescript
  const user = {
    name: 'John',
    email: 'john@example.com',
    role: 'admin',
  };

  const point = { x: 10, y: 20 };
  ```

- section: Comments content: |

  ## 1. Documentation

  ```typescript
  /**
   * Fetches user data from the API
   * @param userId - The ID of the user to fetch
   * @returns The user data object
   */
  const fetchUserData = (userId: string): Promise<UserData> => { ... }
  ```

  ## 2. Style

  - Use `//` for single-line comments, `/* */` for multi-line comments
  - Explain why, not what

  ## 3. TODO

  ```typescript
  // TODO(john): Implement caching for user data
  ```

- section: TypeScript Best Practices content: |

  ## 1. Type Annotations

  ```typescript
  function calculateTotal(items: CartItem[]): number { ... }
  const count = 0;
  ```

  ## 2. Avoid Any

  - Avoid using `any`, prefer explicit types/interfaces

  ## 3. Null and Undefined

  ```typescript
  const username = user?.name ?? 'Anonymous';
  ```

  ## 4. Type Assertion

  ```typescript
  const length = (someValue as string).length;
  ```

- section: React-Specific Patterns content: |

  ## 1. Component Organization

  - One component per file
  - Group by feature folders

  ## 2. Props

  ```typescript
  interface ButtonProps {
    label: string;
    onClick: () => void;
    disabled?: boolean;
  }

  const Button = ({ label, onClick, disabled = false }: ButtonProps) => { ... }
  ```

  ## 3. Hooks

  - Hook names must start with `use`

  ```typescript
  const useUserData = (userId: string) => { ... }
  ```

  ## 4. Client Components

  ```typescript
  'use client';

  import { useState } from 'react';

  export function Counter() {
    const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
    return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>Count: {count}</button>;
  }
  ```

- section: shadcn/ui Components content: |

  ## 1. Import

  ```tsx
  import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';

  <Button variant="outline" size="sm">
    Click me
  </Button>;
  ```

  ## 2. Extend

  ```tsx
  export function ActionButton({ children, ...props }) {
    return (
      <Button variant="default" className="font-bold uppercase" {...props}>
        {children}
      </Button>
    );
  }
  ```

  ## 3. Form Integration

  ```tsx
  import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';

  import { Form, Input } from '@/components/ui/form';
  ```

  ## 4. Notes

  - If new shadcn/ui components are needed, request for addition

- section: Project Structure Overview content: |

  ```
  src/
  ├── app/
  ├── components/
  │   ├── base/
  │   ├── features/
  │   ├── layout/
  │   ├── shared/
  │   └── ui/
  ├── constants/
  ├── core/
  ├── helpers/
  ├── hooks/
  ├── lib/
  ├── messages/
  ├── store/
  ├── styles/
  ├── types/
  └── utils/
  ```

- section: File Naming Conventions content: |

  ## Component Files

  - Use PascalCase, extension `.tsx`

  ## Non-Component Files

  - Use kebab-case (e.g. `format-date.ts`)

  ## Index Files

  - Use `index.ts` or `index.tsx` for exports
